WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:03.430
Next a new study confirms something we already know.

2
00:00:03.430 --> 00:00:05.300
America loves road trips.

3
00:00:05.300 --> 00:00:07.210
Oh, please, yes!

4
00:00:07.210 --> 00:00:08.510
Ugh, again, this is another story

5
00:00:08.510 --> 00:00:09.840
I can get really behind.

6
00:00:09.840 --> 00:00:13.240
People reports a new survey of 2000 drivers

7
00:00:13.240 --> 00:00:17.170
found 76% of them would pick driving over flying

8
00:00:17.170 --> 00:00:19.280
if they knew the drive would be enjoyable.

9
00:00:19.280 --> 00:00:22.300
And 74% said the journey is more important

10
00:00:22.300 --> 00:00:23.290 line:15%
than the destination.

11
00:00:23.290 --> 00:00:26.540 line:15%
And 78% said that they found hidden gems

12
00:00:26.540 --> 00:00:29.380 line:15%
along the way that they would've never found otherwise.

13
00:00:29.380 --> 00:00:32.750 line:15%
And more than half said that the perfect road trip buddy

14
00:00:32.750 --> 00:00:36.170 line:15%
is their partner, that's fortunate.

15
00:00:36.170 --> 00:00:39.560 line:15%
And a lot of people also in this survey said

16
00:00:39.560 --> 00:00:41.370 line:15%
that a spontaneous road trip

17
00:00:41.370 --> 00:00:44.350 line:15%
can be equally if not more enjoyable

18
00:00:44.350 --> 00:00:46.900
than a planned road trip, Ross thoughts?

19
00:00:46.900 --> 00:00:48.350
Well, okay. I wanna be very clear.

20
00:00:48.350 --> 00:00:51.090
I find driving in traffic to be outrageous.

21
00:00:51.090 --> 00:00:52.780
I get stressed out about it.

22
00:00:52.780 --> 00:00:55.600
That being said, I love to dilly and I love to dally.

23
00:00:55.600 --> 00:00:58.190
And so, if we can go on a road trip

24
00:00:58.190 --> 00:01:02.670
and just take our time and explore, sign me up.

25
00:01:02.670 --> 00:01:03.930
Other thing I love about road trips

26
00:01:03.930 --> 00:01:05.650
I thought a lot about this, snacks.

27
00:01:05.650 --> 00:01:08.246
Can we talk about road trip snacks

28
00:01:08.246 --> 00:01:09.400
(audience cheers)

29
00:01:09.400 --> 00:01:11.688
Beef jerky.
Beef jerky.

30
00:01:11.688 --> 00:01:12.521
Beef jerky!

31
00:01:12.521 --> 00:01:14.610
Gimme a big gulp

32
00:01:14.610 --> 00:01:16.490
which I know means we're gonna stop a few times

33
00:01:16.490 --> 00:01:17.323
but I don't care.

34
00:01:17.323 --> 00:01:19.310
I want that big gulp.

35
00:01:19.310 --> 00:01:20.600
I actually have some pictures

36
00:01:20.600 --> 00:01:22.970
of how enthusiastic I am about road trips.

37
00:01:22.970 --> 00:01:25.260
So I'm an RV enthusiast

38
00:01:25.260 --> 00:01:27.430
and this is me when I'm 19 years old,

39
00:01:27.430 --> 00:01:29.760
starting my RV journey.

40
00:01:29.760 --> 00:01:32.320
Yep, that's me and my dog Templeton.

41
00:01:32.320 --> 00:01:33.270
He's long gone.

42
00:01:33.270 --> 00:01:36.500
And that's Nan doing the windshield

43
00:01:36.500 --> 00:01:39.140
because you hit a lot of bugs along the way.

44
00:01:39.140 --> 00:01:43.240
And anyone who can do RVing,

45
00:01:43.240 --> 00:01:48.130
I highly suggest like a classy license, like a Tioga style.

46
00:01:48.130 --> 00:01:50.610
There's two beds, a little table.

47
00:01:50.610 --> 00:01:53.140
You don't have to have a special driver's license for it.

48
00:01:53.140 --> 00:01:57.260
And you just take a map and flip coins at intersections.

49
00:01:57.260 --> 00:01:58.440
Should we go right or left?

50
00:01:58.440 --> 00:02:00.140
I don't know, flip the coin.

51
00:02:00.140 --> 00:02:02.380
It's the greatest thing on earth to do.

52
00:02:02.380 --> 00:02:04.150
And I couldn't recommend it more.

53
00:02:04.150 --> 00:02:05.920
Yeah, Wellie and I,

54
00:02:05.920 --> 00:02:06.930
I actually pitched to him

55
00:02:06.930 --> 00:02:09.480
'cause my fantasy used to go to Winnebago through Montana.

56
00:02:09.480 --> 00:02:10.313
Yes!

57
00:02:10.313 --> 00:02:11.530
And so he said, "What do you think for the honeymoon?"

58
00:02:11.530 --> 00:02:13.600
And we are going to go to Mexico.

59
00:02:13.600 --> 00:02:16.150
Oh (laughs) well, something for everybody.

60
00:02:18.780 --> 00:02:20.009
We'll be right back.

61
00:02:20.009 --> 00:02:22.592 line:15%
(upbeat music)

62
00:02:24.425 --> 00:02:26.387 line:15%
♪ Oh oh oh oh ♪

63
00:02:26.387 --> 00:02:28.271 line:15%
♪ Oh oh oh oh ♪

